Bon Jovi\". *backstage.bonjovi.com*. Retrieved September 22, 2025.\n39. ↑ \"Bon Jovi: Summary\". *TV.com*. CBS Interactive. Archived from the original on March 19, 2012. Retrieved June 1, 2009.\n40. ↑ \"Slippery When Wet – Bon Jovi\". *Billboard*. Retrieved January 13, 2010.\n41. ↑ \"Diamonds Are a 'Chicks' Best Friend\". Recording Industry Association of America. Archived from the original on October 13, 2013. Retrieved September 18, 2012.\n42. 1 2 \"Bon Jovi > Charts & Awards > *Billboard* Singles\". AllMusic. Macrovision. Retrieved July 28, 2009.\n43. ↑ \"1987\". *Billboard*. Archived from the original on July 20, 2015. Retrieved July 18, 2011.\n44. ↑ \"Metrolyrics.com\". Metrolyrics.com. September 11, 1987. Archived from the original on July 22, 2011. Retrieved July 18, 2011.\n45. ↑ \"Rockin' on music awards night\". February 2, 1988. Retrieved July 18, 2011.\n46. ↑ \"1988 Pcavote.com\". Peopleschoice.com. Retrieved July 18, 2011.\n47. ↑ \"69 photos of the legendary Monsters of Rock festival\". *Planet Rock*. Archived from the original on April 25, 2025. Retrieved September 22, 2025.\n48. ↑ Wright, Tracy (June 6, 2022). \"Bon Jovi: A look at the iconic rock band then and now\". Fox News. Retrieved September 22, 2025.\n49. ↑ \"Bon Jovi Songs, Albums, Reviews, Bio & More | ...\" *AllMusic*. Retrieved September 22, 2025.\n50. ↑ \"SS MUSIC > Bon Jovi\". SS MUSIC. Archived from the original on May 30, 2008. Retrieved January 13, 2010.\n51. ↑ \"Bon Jovi Biography > *Billboard.com*\". *Billboard*. Retrieved January 13, 2010.\n52. ↑ Laura Jackson (2010). *Jon Bon Jovi: The Biography*. Hachette. p. 79. ISBN 978-0-7481-2277-6.\n53. ↑ \"On This Day\". *Historyking.com*. Retrieved June 1, 2009.\n54. ↑ Harvilla, Rob (September 7, 2017). \"Nirvana, Lauryn Hill, and Faxes From Don Henley: Behind the Scenes at the Original 'MTV Unplugged'\". *The Ringer*. Retrieved April 22, 2025.\n55. ↑ \"Bon Jovi\". *Melodic-hardrock.com*.\n56. ↑ \"Bon Jovi called in a shrink to solve band issues\". *Daily Express*. October 27, 2009.\n57. ↑ \"Jon Bon Jovi\". *People*. May 6, 1996. Retrieved August 5, 2019.\n58. ↑ \"RIAA Gold & Platinum\". Recording Industry Association of America. Archived from the original on July 11, 2012. Retrieved October 23, 2009.\n59. ↑ \"Chart Archive – Bon Jovi – Cross Road – The Best of\". Official Charts Company. Retrieved May 14, 2012.\n60. ↑ \"Bon Jovi\". *Slow Radio*.\n61. ↑ \"2007 Pcavote.com\". *Peopleschoice.com*. Retrieved July 18, 2011.\n62. ↑ \"MSN.com\". MSN. Archived from the original on October 13, 2008. Retrieved July 18, 2011.\n63. ↑ \"Bon Jovi sell out first Dome gig\". *BBC News*. April 20, 2007. Retrieved July 8, 2009.\n64. ↑ \"2008 Winners\". CMT. 2008. Archived from the original on January 29, 2010. Retrieved April 7, 2009.\n65. ↑ \"Backstage With Rascal Flatts, LeAnn Rimes, Robert Plant and Alison Krauss\". CMT. April 16, 2008. Archived from the original on April 20, 2008. Retrieved April 7, 2009.\n66. ↑ \"43rd Academy of Country Music Awards\". CBS. Archived from the original on March 22, 2009. Retrieved April 7, 2009.\n67. 1 2 Waddell, Ray (December 11, 2008). \"Bon Jovi Scores 2008's Top-Grossing Tour\". *Billboard*. Retrieved December 13, 2008.\n68. ↑ \"Madonna biggest 2008 North American tour attraction\". Yahoo! News. Reuters. December 30, 2008. Archived from the original on January 1, 2009. Retrieved December 31, 2008.\n69. ↑ \"Bon Jovi Announces Meadowlands Concerts\". *Billboard*. Retrieved December 30, 2009.\n70. ↑ \"Bon Jovi world tour tops ticket sales in tough '10\". Standard.net. Archived from the original on May 11, 2012. Retrieved March 20, 2013.\n71. ↑ \"Bon Jovi ($125 million) – The World's 25 Highest-Paid Musicians 2011\". *Forbes*. June 15, 2011. Retrieved March 20, 2013.\n72. ↑ \"Top 25 Tours of 2011\". *Billboard*. December 8, 2011. Archived from the original on December 27, 2011. Retrieved December 27, 2011.\n73. ↑ \"note from JBJ\". Archived from the original on February 20, 2012. Re